# Statistics Portugal (INE, Instituto Nacional de Estatística) publishes the official statistics of Portugal 
# through its indicator API. These fields read about a hundred of its indicators: population, births and deaths, 
# housing and rents, prices, wages and jobs, tourism, businesses, foreign trade, crime, health, education, 
# environment and agriculture. Each field returns the values of one indicator for one period, by place and by 
# the indicator's other categories. A generator outside the repository writes this file and ine/indicators.json; 
# the names and descriptions are written for the model.

extend type Query {
    """
    The resident population of a place on 31 December, by sex and age group. The latest year is 2023, and one
    request returns one year.
    """
    inePopulation(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place in INE's 2013 codes, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. Lisboa is 1701106 here. A
        place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        sex: String
        """
        The age group: T for all, or five years such as 11 for 0 to 4, 12 for 5 to 9, 21 for 10 to 14, up to
        92 for 85 and over.
        """
        ageGroup: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    How many shops, clinics, offices and other sites of a kind a place has: the establishments in the place,
    by economic activity and legal form. Activity 75000 is veterinary activities: pet clinics, vet clinics and
    veterinary hospitals. 47762 is pet shops, 01493 pet breeders, and 96092 pet care services such as
    grooming, pet sitting, training and boarding. A business can run several sites, so there are more
    establishments than enterprises (ineEnterprises).
    """
    ineEstablishments(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The economic activity as a CAE Rev. 3 code: TOT for all, a section letter such as G for trade or I for
        accommodation and food, or a five-digit subclass such as 75000 for pet clinics, 96092 for pet care
        services, 56101 for restaurants or 47111 for supermarkets. A name, such as veterinary activities or
        pet care, works as well as a code.
        """
        activity: String
        "The legal form: T for all, 1 for sole proprietors, 2 for companies."
        legalForm: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    How many businesses of a kind a place has, such as pet shops, pet clinics, restaurants or hotels: the
    enterprises based in the place, by economic activity and legal form. Activity 75000 is veterinary
    activities: pet clinics, vet clinics and veterinary hospitals. 47762 is pet shops, 01493 pet breeders, and
    96092 pet care services such as grooming, pet sitting, training and boarding. A business can run several
    sites, which ineEstablishments counts one by one.
    """
    ineEnterprises(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The economic activity as a CAE Rev. 3 code: TOT for all, a section letter such as G for trade or I for
        accommodation and food, or a five-digit subclass such as 75000 for pet clinics, 96092 for pet care
        services, 56101 for restaurants or 47111 for supermarkets. A name, such as veterinary activities or
        pet care, works as well as a code.
        """
        businessActivity: String
        "The legal form: T for all, 1 for sole proprietors, 2 for companies."
        businessLegalForm: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The crimes registered by the police in a place, by category of crime. Category 10 is crimes against pet
    animals: killing, ill-treatment and abandonment of pets.
    """
    ineCrimes(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The category of crime: T for all, 1 for crimes against persons, 12194 for domestic violence, 2 for
        crimes against property, 2831_2832 for theft of or from a car, 41682 for drunk driving, 10 for crimes
        against pet animals.
        """
        crimeCategory: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The change of consumer prices from the same month a year earlier, in percent, by COICOP category: T for
    all goods and services (the inflation rate), 0945 for veterinary and other services for pets (the price of
    a pet clinic visit), 0932 for pets and pet products. The latest month comes out about six weeks after it
    ends.
    """
    ineConsumerPriceChange(
        "The month, written as year and month, such as 2026-09. Leave it out for the latest month."
        month: String
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal or 1 for the mainland. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its
        code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The COICOP category: T for all, 01 for food and drinks, 04 for housing and energy, 07 for transport,
        11 for restaurants and hotels, 0945 for veterinary and other services for pets, 0932 for pets and pet
        products.
        """
        priceCategory: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The number of enterprises in Portugal by economic activity in the CAE Rev. 4 classification and by number
    of persons employed, from 2024. Subclass 96992 is pet care services: grooming, pet sitting, training and
    boarding. For 2023 and earlier, ineEnterprises gives pet care under its CAE Rev. 3 code, 96092.
    """
    ineEnterprisesCaeRev4(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, the only place of this indicator. A place's name, such as Porto, works as
        well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The economic activity as a CAE Rev. 4 code: TOT for all, or a subclass such as 96992 for pet care
        services, 75000 for veterinary activities (pet clinics), 47762 for pet shops or 01483 for pet
        breeders. T is the section of other services. A name, such as veterinary activities or pet care, works
        as well as a code.
        """
        activityRev4: String
        """
        The persons employed: T for all sizes, 1 for fewer than 10, 2 for 10 to 49, 3 for 50 to 249, 4 for 250
        or more.
        """
        sizeClass: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The imports of goods into Portugal in euros, by country of origin and product, one year at a time: which
    countries Portugal buys a product from, and for how much. A product is a Combined Nomenclature code, such
    as 230910 for dog or cat food, 2204 for wine or 0302 for fresh fish, or its name. Leave place out to get
    every country: the rows mix countries with totals such as MUNDO (World) and INTRA (the European Union),
    and the countries are the rows whose place code has two letters.
    """
    ineImports(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The country the goods come from, as a two-letter code, such as IT for Italy or CN for China, or MUNDO
        for the world. Portugal is the country they go to. Leave it out for every country and total.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The product as a Combined Nomenclature code, digits without dots, such as 230910 for dog or cat food
        put up for retail sale, a chapter such as 23, or T for all goods. A name, such as dog or cat food or
        pet care, works as well as a code.
        """
        importedProduct: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The resident population of Portugal and its regions on 31 December, by sex and age, up to 2025. For a
    municipality, use inePopulation.
    """
    inePopulationByRegion(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, 1 for the mainland, or a region such as 11 for Norte or 1A for Grande
        Lisboa. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        regionalSex: String
        """
        The age: T for all, five years such as 11 for 0 to 4 or 92 for 85 and over, or one year such as 224
        for 18.
        """
        age: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    "The population density of a place, in inhabitants per square kilometre. The latest year is 2025."
    inePopulationDensity(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The ageing ratio of a place: residents aged 65 and over for every 100 residents under 15. The latest year
    is 2025.
    """
    ineAgeingRatio(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The old-age dependency ratio of a place: residents aged 65 and over for every 100 residents aged 15 to 64.
    The latest year is 2025.
    """
    ineOldAgeDependencyRatio(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The net migration of a place in a year: the people who moved in, from Portugal or abroad, minus those who
    moved out. The latest year is 2025.
    """
    ineNetMigration(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The permanent immigrants to Portugal in a year: people who came from abroad to live for at least a year,
    by sex, age and nationality.
    """
    ineImmigrants(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, the only place of this indicator. A place's name, such as Porto, works as
        well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        immigrantSex: String
        """
        The age: T for all, five years such as 11 for 0 to 4 or 92 for 85 and over, or one year such as 224
        for 18.
        """
        immigrantAge: String
        "The nationality: T for all, PT for Portuguese, EST for foreign."
        nationality: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The permanent emigrants from Portugal in a year: residents who left to live abroad for at least a year, by
    sex.
    """
    ineEmigrants(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, the only place of this indicator. A place's name, such as Porto, works as
        well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        emigrantSex: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The foreign citizens living in Portugal with a legal residence status, by sex. The latest year is 2023.
    """
    ineForeignResidents(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, the only place of this indicator. A place's name, such as Porto, works as
        well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        foreignResidentSex: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The resident population counted by the 2021 census, down to the parish, by sex. The census year 2021 is
    the only year.
    """
    ineCensusPopulation(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The census code of the place: PT for Portugal, 11A for the Porto area, 1312 for Porto, or a parish
        such as 131210 for Paranhos. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        censusSex: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The private households counted by the 2021 census, down to the parish, by type of living quarters. The
    census year 2021 is the only year.
    """
    ineCensusHouseholds(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The census code of the place: PT for Portugal, 11A for the Porto area, 1312 for Porto, or a parish
        such as 131210 for Paranhos. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        """
        The type of living quarters: T for all, 1 for housing units, 2 for collective living quarters such as
        care homes.
        """
        livingQuarters: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The crude birth rate of a place: live births in the year for every 1,000 residents. The latest year is
    2025.
    """
    ineBirthRate(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The live births of a month by the mother's place of residence and the baby's sex. It covers the months of
    the current year.
    """
    ineMonthlyBirths(
        "The month, written as year and month, such as 2026-09. Leave it out for the latest month."
        month: String
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, down to the subregion, such as PT for Portugal, 11 for Norte or 11A for the Porto
        metropolitan area. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The baby's sex: T for both, 1 for boys, 2 for girls."
        babySex: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The live births of a year by the mother's place of residence, down to the parish, and by the baby's sex.
    The latest year is 2023.
    """
    ineBirths(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place in INE's 2013 codes, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. Lisboa is 1701106 here. A
        place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The baby's sex: T for both, 1 for boys, 2 for girls."
        newbornSex: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    "The live births in Portugal to mothers aged 19 or younger, by the mother's age."
    ineTeenageBirths(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place: PT for Portugal, the only place of this indicator. A place's name, such as Porto, works as
        well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The mother's age: T for 19 or younger, 01 for 11 years, 02 for 12, and so on up to 09 for 19 years."
        motherAge: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The deaths of residents of Portugal and its regions, by sex, age group and day of death. The count for the
    current year is partial and grows each month.
    """
    ineDeaths(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, down to the region, such as PT for Portugal, 1 for the mainland or 11 for Norte. A place's
        name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The sex: T for both, 1 for men, 2 for women."
        deceasedSex: String
        """
        The age group: T for all, 00 for under 65, 01 for 65 to 69, 02 for 70 to 74, 03 for 75 to 79, 04 for
        80 to 84, 05 for 85 or over.
        """
        deathAgeGroup: String
        "The date: T for the year, a month such as 01 for January, or a day such as 0115 for 15 January."
        dayOfDeath: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The crude death rate of a place: deaths in the year for every 1,000 residents. The latest year is 2023.
    """
    ineDeathRate(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place in INE's 2013 codes, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. Lisboa is 1701106 here. A
        place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The death rate from cancer (malignant tumours) in a place: deaths for every 1,000 residents. The latest
    year is 2024.
    """
    ineCancerDeathRate(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The median rent of the new lease contracts for dwellings signed in a year, in euros per square metre per
    month, down to the parish. The latest year is 2024.
    """
    ineMedianRent(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
