        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The number of new lease contracts for dwellings signed in a year, down to the parish. The latest year is
    2024.
    """
    ineNewLeases(
        """
        The year of the values. Leave it out for the latest year. For several years, make one request for each
        year, or set allPeriods.
        """
        year: Int
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, down to the parish, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the
        codes. A place's name, such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The median value that banks put on homes when they assess them for a mortgage, in euros per square metre,
    by type of home. It tracks house prices month by month.
    """
    ineBankValuation(
        "The month, written as year and month, such as 2026-09. Leave it out for the latest month."
        month: String
        """
        True for every period INE has, which can be a long list. The answer has one observation for each
        period, so select period to know which period each value is for.
        """
        allPeriods: Boolean = false
        """
        The place, such as PT for Portugal or 11A1312 for Porto. inePlaces gives the codes. A place's name,
        such as Porto, works as well as its code.
        """
        place: String
        "The type of home: T for all, 1 for flats, 2 for houses."
        homeType: String
    ): [IneObservation!]

    """
    The number of conventional dwellings (homes) that exist in a place, from INE's housing stock estimates.
    The latest year is 2022.
    """
